1
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:06,130
Kaede-san!

2
00:00:06,130 --> 00:00:08,340
Hi, Minato.

3
00:00:08,340 --> 00:00:10,180
Can I sit here?

4
00:00:10,180 --> 00:00:11,390
Sure!

5
00:00:13,260 --> 00:00:15,390
What are you reading?

6
00:00:16,980 --> 00:00:18,980
Romeo and Juliet.

7
00:00:18,980 --> 00:00:20,940
It's also by Shakespeare.

8
00:00:20,940 --> 00:00:23,020
I've heard of it.

9
00:00:23,520 --> 00:00:25,320
This book...

10
00:00:25,320 --> 00:00:27,780
It's how Haru and I started dating.

11
00:00:29,320 --> 00:00:30,910
We got so into our roles back then,

12
00:00:30,910 --> 00:00:31,910
and one thing led to another.

13
00:00:33,070 --> 00:00:35,620
Oh, I see.

14
00:00:35,620 --> 00:00:36,490
But then...

15
00:00:36,490 --> 00:00:38,080
He wanted to focus on theater,

16
00:00:38,080 --> 00:00:40,120
so he dumped me.

17
00:00:40,120 --> 00:00:41,250
What?!

18
00:00:41,250 --> 00:00:43,330
You two broke up?

19
00:00:43,330 --> 00:00:45,750
A year ago, actually.

20
00:00:46,710 --> 00:00:48,760
Haru is a total theater geek.

21
00:00:52,550 --> 00:00:54,430
Honestly,

22
00:00:54,430 --> 00:00:55,560
the role of Viola...

23
00:00:55,560 --> 00:00:58,350
should have gone to you, Kaede-san.

24
00:00:58,350 --> 00:00:59,640
Huh?

25
00:01:00,480 --> 00:01:01,190
I mean,

26
00:01:01,190 --> 00:01:03,730
compared to your passion,
I really don't measure up.

27
00:01:04,940 --> 00:01:06,690
Don't say that.

28
00:01:06,690 --> 00:01:08,690
Why do you say that?

29
00:01:09,150 --> 00:01:11,070
The one Haru chose to play Viola

30
00:01:11,740 --> 00:01:13,820
wasn't me. It was you.

31
00:01:26,090 --> 00:01:29,920
Mmm, this is delicious!

32
00:01:29,920 --> 00:01:31,550
What's wrong? Aren't you eating?

33
00:01:31,550 --> 00:01:32,760
I'm taking this, then.

34
00:01:37,510 --> 00:01:38,510
What's on your mind?

35
00:01:38,680 --> 00:01:40,350
I just...

36
00:01:40,350 --> 00:01:43,190
feel like Viola should
be played by Kaede-san.

37
00:01:43,810 --> 00:01:45,110
Why do you think that?

38
00:01:45,110 --> 00:01:46,610
Because...

39
00:01:46,610 --> 00:01:48,860
Kaede-san is a much better actor,

40
00:01:48,860 --> 00:01:50,490
and she's beautiful...

41
00:01:50,490 --> 00:01:51,950
Does being a good actor

42
00:01:51,950 --> 00:01:54,410
and being beautiful

43
00:01:54,410 --> 00:01:55,870
mean you're the only one who can play Viola?

44
00:01:55,870 --> 00:01:57,410
I don't know...

45
00:01:57,780 --> 00:01:59,790
- But compared to me, Kaede-san is...
- That's true!

46
00:01:59,790 --> 00:02:01,660
Kaede is an excellent actress.

47
00:02:01,660 --> 00:02:02,620
But in you,

48
00:02:02,620 --> 00:02:03,410
I saw something

49
00:02:03,410 --> 00:02:04,370
that goes beyond acting.

50
00:02:04,370 --> 00:02:05,750
Something special.

51
00:02:06,290 --> 00:02:07,790
What do you mean?

52
00:02:08,210 --> 00:02:10,880
The first time I heard your voice,

53
00:02:10,880 --> 00:02:13,260
it was as if Viola herself
had appeared right before me.

54
00:02:13,760 --> 00:02:15,510
It felt like Viola

55
00:02:15,510 --> 00:02:16,930
was truly alive right there.

56
00:02:21,430 --> 00:02:24,640
"Our destiny is not in the stars."

57
00:02:24,640 --> 00:02:27,190
You were holding this back then, too.

58
00:02:27,190 --> 00:02:28,270
That line...

59
00:02:28,940 --> 00:02:30,360
what does it mean to you?

60
00:02:34,950 --> 00:02:36,910
Hey.

61
00:02:36,910 --> 00:02:39,700
What's wrong?

62
00:02:39,700 --> 00:02:42,620
Talk to me.

63
00:02:42,620 --> 00:02:44,540
This is...
